From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the desktop to one remote seat at a time

Upstream places no limit on concurrent connections, and each one brings its own
virtual monitor, so a second client extends the desktop instead of taking it
over. Close every incumbent when a new connection is activated, and activate
the new one immediately rather than waiting for the incumbent to actually
finish tearing down first.

An earlier version of this same idea polled the incumbent's teardown for up to
10 seconds before activating, on the theory that KRdp's own session creation
needed the old seat fully released first. Measurement showed otherwise:
activating immediately after close() - even while the incumbent's own
teardown is still in flight - completes cleanly, including a successful
output-lifecycle "up", well under a second later. The only thing with a real
exclusivity requirement is the lifecycle helper's own brief settling window,
and it already waits that out itself; gating session creation on it a second
time here only added dead time; that dead time, not the momentary two-output
overlap itself, is what produced the black screen.

diff --git a/server/SessionController.cpp b/server/SessionController.cpp
index 8f352ef..3471c3f 100644
--- a/server/SessionController.cpp
+++ b/server/SessionController.cpp
@@ -248,6 +248,30 @@ void SessionController::onNewConnection(KRdp::RdpConnection *newConnection)
             return;
         }
 
+        // One remote seat. Upstream places no limit on concurrent connections
+        // and each one brings its own virtual monitor, so a second client
+        // extends the desktop instead of taking it over.
+        //
+        // Close every incumbent and activate the new connection in the same
+        // tick, without waiting for the incumbent to actually finish tearing
+        // down first. An earlier version of this polled m_wrappers for up to
+        // 10s before activating, on the theory that KRdp's own session
+        // creation needed the old one gone. It did not: activating
+        // immediately after close() - even while the incumbent's own
+        // teardown was still in flight - was observed to complete cleanly,
+        // including a successful output-lifecycle "up", well under a second
+        // later. The only thing with a real exclusivity requirement is the
+        // lifecycle helper's own brief settling window, which it already
+        // waits out itself; gating session creation on it a second time here
+        // only added dead time, and that dead time is what produced the
+        // black screen - not the momentary two-output overlap itself.
+        for (const auto &incumbent : m_wrappers) {
+            if (incumbent->connection && incumbent->connection != newConnection) {
+                qInfo() << "KRDP-SEAT: closing incumbent session" << incumbent->connection << "for" << newConnection;
+                incumbent->connection->close();
+            }
+        }
+
         auto wrapper = std::make_unique<SessionWrapper>(newConnection, makeSession(), m_sni);
         // 6.8 never looks at the client's own desktop: an explicit
         // --virtual-monitor wins, and otherwise a fixed 1024x768 is used. By
